\cf2 Three literatures, one pathology: \strokec3 a single anchor cannot survive reformulation of its context.\strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa30\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 C10\strokec5 : write anchored at one token (last prompt), one band, one value. Paraphrase 0/72. Hidden-state transfer 0.8\'961.8% at any ridge \'97 the anchor simply isn't reconstructed by the reformulated prompt.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Na\'efve RAG\strokec5 : one index (dense or sparse). Query reformulation moves the embedding off the anchor; recall collapses. The RAGPart/RAGMask finding is the dual \'97 retrieval anchors on literal tokens, not task structure, which is exactly your keygram rank-1.02 collapse in a different currency.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Autoregressive video\strokec5 : context anchored on the tail alone. Error accumulates over rollout because short-term continuity is the only anchor there is.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The naming in your own graph is almost embarrassing: `edit \uc0\u8596  single` carries the labels \strokec5 paraphrase, token, subject, multus, band\strokec4 . The single/multus axis is the live variable, and it's categorical.\
