\cf2 \strokec3 What the two solved cases did\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Hybrid RAG (Blended RAG, HyPA-RAG, HetaRAG).\strokec4  They did not tune a single retriever harder. They refused to pick one index: dense + sparse + KG, blended by a \strokec3 query-complexity classifier\strokec4  that routes adaptively. The gain comes from \strokec5 heterogeneous anchors with a routing rule\strokec4  \'97 not from better anchors.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Relax Forcing.\strokec4  Three \strokec5 functionally distinct\strokec4  roles: Sink (global stability), Tail (short-term continuity), History (mid-range motion). The selection criterion is the sharp part \'97 History frames are chosen to \strokec3 maximise alignment with global anchors while suppressing redundancy with recent context\strokec4 . That is a diversity objective over memory slots, training-free.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Both are the same move: \strokec3 role-decompose the anchor, add a selection rule that penalises redundancy.\strokec4 \
